Subject: [PATCH 06/13] Fix out-of-bounds write in checkUiccListenConfigNeeded

The `RoutingManager::checkUiccListenConfigNeeded` function lacked validation for the `nb_config` index against the maximum supported execution environments (`NFA_EE_MAX_EE_SUPPORTED`). If the maximum number of execution environments was exceeded, this flaw allowed an out-of-bounds write, potentially corrupting adjacent synchronization primitives and causing process crashes or deadlocks within the NFC system service.

This commit resolves the issue by adding a bounds check before appending a new UICC listen configuration. If `nb_config` reaches `NFA_EE_MAX_EE_SUPPORTED`, the function now logs an error and returns false, preventing the out-of-bounds array access. A new unit test is also introduced to ensure the overflow condition is handled safely.

Test: atest RoutingManagerTest

